                <pb facs="0210" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg114"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure C in No. 53.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>Small-pox is raging with unabated vigor in Santiago and the adjoining districts,
                    but the energetic measures adopted by the Intendente, and in which he has been
                    nobly seconded by his fellow-citizens and many foreigners, notably among the
                    latter the United States minister, the Hon. J. P. Root, are beginning to tell
                    favorably, for, although there is little or no diminution in the number of
                    cases, there is a decrease in the rate of mortality.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
